   "op": "replace_brief",
   "brief": "dvt",
   "html": "<div class=\"brief sp\" id=\"dvt\" data-entry=\"disease\" data-lens=\"fm\" data-spine=\"2\" data-shelf=\"fm\" data-bp=\"cv heme\">\n<h4>Venous Thromboembolism</h4>\n<p class=\"sub\">pretest probability governs the test &middot; D-dimer only rules out &middot; imaging by stability &middot; swollen-leg mimics</p>\n<nav class=\"sp-step\" aria-label=\"Decision spine\"><a href=\"#ve-s1\"><b>1</b><span>Script</span></a><a href=\"#ve-s2\"><b>2</b><span>Urgent</span></a><a href=\"#ve-s3\"><b>3</b><span>Differential</span></a><a href=\"#ve-s4\"><b>4</b><span>Workup</span></a><a href=\"#ve-s5\"><b>5</b><span>Criteria</span></a><a href=\"#ve-s6\"><b>6</b><span>Severity</span></a><a href=\"#ve-s7\"><b>7</b><span>Treatment</span></a><a href=\"#ve-s8\"><b>8</b><span>Follow-up</span></a><a href=\"#dvt-s151-bank\" class=\"sp-prac\"><span>Practice</span></a></nav>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"ve-s1\"><b class=\"sp-n\">1</b>Illness script</h5>\n<div class=\"dp\"><span class=\"lbl\">Bottom line</span><ul class=\"bl\"><li><b>Pretest probability</b> selects the test: <b>D-dimer rules out</b> in a low-probability patient; <b>high probability goes directly to imaging</b>. A positive D-dimer does not confirm a clot.</li><li><b>Unstable suspected pulmonary embolism (PE): bedside echocardiography</b> and urgent treatment; <b>hemodynamic compromise</b> can require thrombolysis when no contraindication is present.</li><li>Treat most confirmed proximal deep vein thrombosis (DVT) or PE with <b>anticoagulation for at least 3 months</b>; persistent or unprovoked risk may justify longer treatment.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"sp-script sp-s2\"><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">What it is</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Venous thromboembolism (VTE): a venous clot, usually in the leg or pelvis, that may embolize to a pulmonary artery.</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Driver</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Virchow triad: venous stasis, endothelial injury and hypercoagulability.</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Triggers</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Immobility, surgery or trauma; cancer, pregnancy, estrogen exposure or inherited thrombophilia.</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Chain</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>A venous thrombus obstructs flow; embolization can cause pulmonary vascular obstruction and hypotension.</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Insights</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>D-dimer can rise with inflammation, pregnancy, surgery or cancer; it is not a rule-in test.</p><p>A palpable superficial cord or a bruised calf after sudden pain can point to a DVT mimic.</p></div></div></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"ve-s2\"><b class=\"sp-n\">2</b>Urgent risks</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Hemodynamic instability</caption><thead><tr><th>Finding</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Suspected PE with hypotension or shock</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Arrange urgent bedside assessment of the right ventricle with echocardiography; stabilize and treat without delaying for an unsafe CT transfer.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>PE causing hemodynamic compromise</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Give thrombolysis if appropriate and no contraindication exists; consider catheter or surgical treatment when thrombolysis is unsuitable.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Massive painful leg swelling with cyanosis or ischemia: phlegmasia</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Arrange urgent vascular assessment and treatment to prevent venous gangrene.</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"ve-s3\"><b class=\"sp-n\">3</b>Differential</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>The swollen leg</caption><thead><tr><th>Diagnosis</th><th>Decides it</th><th>Next best step</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>DVT</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Diffuse unilateral swelling with thrombotic risk and calf tenderness.</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Estimate probability; obtain compression ultrasound when indicated.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"cellulitis\">Skin and Soft Tissue Infection</button></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Fever with spreading skin erythema and a portal of entry.</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Treat the skin infection after assessing whether DVT also needs exclusion.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Ruptured Baker cyst</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\"><b>Sudden</b> calf pain with knee disease; bruising can track below the malleolus.</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Use ultrasound if the distinction from DVT remains uncertain.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Superficial thrombophlebitis</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">A tender, palpable cord along a superficial vein.</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Order duplex ultrasound if associated DVT is clinically suspected.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Chronic venous insufficiency</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\"><b>Chronic:</b> dependent swelling, worse with standing, and hemosiderin staining.</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Order duplex ultrasound if an acute clot remains clinically plausible.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Lymphedema</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Painless, often non-pitting swelling involving the dorsal foot; a positive Stemmer sign.</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Exclude DVT with ultrasound if suspected, then evaluate a lymphatic cause.</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"ve-s4\"><b class=\"sp-n\">4</b>Workup</h5>\n<figure class=\"lcp w5a\"><p class=\"kick\">Diagnostic workup</p><p class=\"w5z\">First step</p><div class=\"w5t first\"><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Symptoms of DVT or PE</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Assess clinical probability and hemodynamic stability</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Low probability and suitable for rule-out testing</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1\"><span class=\"mask\">Use D-dimer; a negative result can exclude VTE in the appropriate setting.</span></div><div class=\"w5fd fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">High probability</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m fl\"><span class=\"mask\">Proceed directly to the appropriate imaging test.</span></div></div></div><p class=\"w5z\">Targeted tests</p><div class=\"w5t\"><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Stable, low clinical risk for PE</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Pulmonary embolism rule-out criteria (PERC)</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1 fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">All eight low-risk criteria met</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1 fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1 fl\"><span class=\"mask\">No PE testing is needed.</span></div></div><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Leg swelling with moderate or high DVT probability, or a positive D-dimer</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Compression ultrasound with Doppler</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1 fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">A noncompressible deep vein</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1 fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1 fl\"><span class=\"mask\">Confirms DVT; begin appropriate treatment.</span></div></div><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Stable suspected PE with high probability or a positive D-dimer</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">CT pulmonary angiography</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1 fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Pulmonary arterial filling defect</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1 fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1 fl\"><span class=\"mask\">Confirms PE; anticoagulate when appropriate.</span></div></div><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">Iodinated contrast is unsuitable, including significant renal insufficiency</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Ventilation/perfusion (V/Q) scan</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1 fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">High-probability or normal scan</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1 fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1 fl\"><span class=\"mask\">A normal scan excludes PE; a high-probability scan supports PE when the clinical probability agrees. A nondiagnostic scan needs leg duplex or further imaging; a negative leg study does not exclude PE.</span></div></div></div><p class=\"w5skip\"><span class=\"w5z\">Skip</span><span class=\"mask\">Do not use a positive D-dimer as confirmation, or delay high-probability imaging while waiting for D-dimer.</span></p></figure>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Clues that change the answer</caption><thead><tr><th>Clue</th><th>Points to</th><th>Next best step</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Low probability and negative D-dimer</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">VTE can be excluded in the appropriate setting</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Stop the clot-testing branch.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>High probability</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">D-dimer is not the next test</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Order imaging.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Pregnancy and suspected PE</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Imaging selection depends on the clinical context</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Consider V/Q imaging when suitable, especially with a normal chest radiograph.</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"sp-pause\"><b class=\"pp-t\">Pause point</b>\n<div class=\"pp-b\">\n<span class=\"sl\">Suspected VTE with a positive D-dimer</span>\n<span class=\"si pp-off\">Read as <em>established VTE</em></span>\n<span class=\"si\"><span class=\"mask\">A positive D-dimer does not establish VTE</span></span>\n<span class=\"pp-a\">&rarr; <span class=\"mask\">Separate clot probability from stability</span></span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pp-b\">\n<span class=\"sl\">Unstable patient with suspected VTE</span>\n<span class=\"si pp-off\">Offered: <em>waiting for CT</em></span>\n<span class=\"si\"><span class=\"mask\">Unstable</span></span>\n<span class=\"pp-a\">&rarr; <span class=\"mask\">May be unable to wait for CT</span></span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"ve-s5\"><b class=\"sp-n\">5</b>Diagnostic criteria</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Confirmation</caption><thead><tr><th>Site</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>DVT</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">A noncompressible vein on ultrasound.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>PE</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">A pulmonary arterial filling defect on CT angiography; use an alternative diagnostic pathway when contrast is unsuitable.</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"ve-s6\"><b class=\"sp-n\">6</b>Severity</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Treatment branch</caption><thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hemodynamically stable</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Anticoagulate appropriate confirmed events; if PE is strongly suspected and bleeding risk is low, begin while confirmation is pending.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Hemodynamic compromise</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Assess urgently for reperfusion treatment.</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"ve-s7\"><b class=\"sp-n\">7</b>Treatment</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-ladder\" aria-label=\"Treatment ladder\"><div class=\"sp-rung\"><span class=\"sp-node\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1</span><div class=\"sp-rb\"><p class=\"sp-when\"><b>Anticoagulation</b><span>Stable proximal DVT or PE</span></p><p><span class=\"mask\">Rivaroxaban or apixaban can be started without heparin bridging in suitable patients. Heparin followed by warfarin is an alternative.</span></p></div></div><div class=\"sp-rung\"><span class=\"sp-node\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2</span><div class=\"sp-rb\"><p class=\"sp-when\"><b>Choose by context</b><span>Pregnancy or important renal impairment</span></p><p><span class=\"mask\">Use low-molecular-weight heparin (LMWH) in pregnancy; warfarin is teratogenic. Unfractionated heparin may be preferred initially with renal insufficiency; assess the full clinical setting.</span></p></div></div><div class=\"sp-rung\"><span class=\"sp-node\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3</span><div class=\"sp-rb\"><p class=\"sp-when\"><b>Duration</b><span>After the initial treatment phase</span></p><p><span class=\"mask\">The initial course for most proximal events is 3 to 6 months. A major transient provoking factor commonly permits stopping after 3 months; consider extended treatment for unprovoked, recurrent or persistent-risk events after weighing bleeding risk.</span></p></div></div><div class=\"sp-rung\"><span class=\"sp-node\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4</span><div class=\"sp-rb\"><p class=\"sp-when\"><b>Caution</b><span>Anticoagulation contraindicated</span></p><p><span class=\"mask\">Consider a temporary inferior vena cava (IVC) filter. Recurrent PE despite adequate anticoagulation is a selected additional indication, rather than a routine alternative to anticoagulation.</span></p></div></div></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"ve-s8\"><b class=\"sp-n\">8</b>Follow-up</h5>\n<figure class=\"lcw\"> <div class=\"ttl\"> <span>Anticoagulation phases</span> <small style=\"font-size:11px\">not to scale</small> </div> <ol class=\"wrows\"> <li class=\"wr\"> <div class=\"wh\"> <b class=\"nm mask\">Initial treatment</b> <span class=\"win\">At least 3 months for most proximal events</span> </div> <div class=\"wb\"> <div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> <i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"> </i> <i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:56%\"> </i> <i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:98%\"> </i> <i class=\"bar c1\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:56%\"> </i> </div> <div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> <span class=\"a0\" style=\"font-size:11px;--x:0%\">Start</span> <span class=\"\" style=\"font-size:11px;--x:56%\">3 months</span> <span class=\"a1\" style=\"font-size:11px;--x:98%\">Later</span> <em>&rarr;</em> </div> </div> </li> <li class=\"wr\"> <div class=\"wh\"> <b class=\"nm mask\">Extended treatment</b> <span class=\"win\">Selected unprovoked, recurrent or persistent-risk events</span> </div> <div class=\"wb\"> <div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> <i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"> </i> <i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:56%\"> </i> <i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:98%\"> </i> <i class=\"bar c3\" style=\"--a:56%;--b:98%\"> </i> </div> <div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> <span class=\"a0\" style=\"font-size:11px;--x:0%\">Start</span> <span class=\"\" style=\"font-size:11px;--x:56%\">3 months</span> <span class=\"a1\" style=\"font-size:11px;--x:98%\">Later</span> <em>&rarr;</em> </div> </div> </li> </ol> </figure>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Reassessment</caption><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>Do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Before stopping or extending anticoagulation</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Reassess provoking factors, recurrence risk, bleeding risk and patient preferences.</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Persistent leg symptoms after DVT</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Assess for post-thrombotic syndrome and chronic venous complications.</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n<h5 class=\"authored-hdr\" id=\"dvt-s151-bank\">Scenario bank</h5>\n<ol class=\"bank authored\">\n<li data-type=\"test\" data-d1=\"D-dimer first\" data-d2=\"CT venography\" data-item-id=\"q_83895e5d5e895246a563\" data-item-version=\"2\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_f9540a7c0eed5f9db679\" data-d1-id=\"o_16ed86b351885e27993a\" data-d2-id=\"o_b26f544aa4805838a0e2\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most appropriate diagnostic study to obtain at this time?\" data-key-why=\"High DVT probability goes directly to compression ultrasound.\" data-d1-why=\"D-dimer is a rule-out test for lower-probability presentations.\" data-d2-why=\"Compression ultrasound is the standard first imaging test.\">62 yo F, unilateral leg swelling with a high Wells score → <b>Compression ultrasound</b> → skip the D-dimer</li>\n<li data-type=\"test\" data-d1=\"CT pulmonary angiography\" data-d2=\"V/Q scan\" data-item-id=\"q_ecf3c27530465348bfb3\" data-item-version=\"2\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_c04bf874f7bb57b3a47f\" data-d1-id=\"o_7326a8a878c653c0892b\" data-d2-id=\"o_58d40601eac05716b394\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most appropriate diagnostic study to obtain at this time?\" data-key-why=\"A negative D-dimer can exclude PE at low pretest probability.\" data-d1-why=\"Immediate CT can be avoided by an appropriate rule-out pathway.\" data-d2-why=\"V/Q imaging is not the first test in this low-probability rule-out branch.\">34 yo F with pleuritic chest pain and low pretest probability → <b>D-dimer to rule out</b></li>\n<li data-type=\"test\" data-d1=\"CT pulmonary angiography\" data-d2=\"D-dimer\" data-item-id=\"q_18d1b7f8019e56b9bf57\" data-item-version=\"2\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_4fad007597035a5c9a64\" data-d1-id=\"o_d0059a6a2da45da0aca3\" data-d2-id=\"o_c027de1ea203569db514\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most appropriate diagnostic study to obtain at this time?\" data-key-why=\"V/Q scanning avoids iodinated contrast when renal function makes CT contrast unsuitable.\" data-d1-why=\"Iodinated contrast is problematic with significant renal insufficiency.\" data-d2-why=\"D-dimer does not confirm PE or replace needed imaging.\">62 yo F with suspected PE and creatinine 3.2 → <b>V/Q scan</b></li>\n<li data-type=\"next\" data-d1=\"CT pulmonary angiography first\" data-d2=\"Anticoagulation alone\" data-item-id=\"q_a17d665b4b1e5860bbfa\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_d98dc576f2da57a68874\" data-d1-id=\"o_189c04269cd956409528\" data-d2-id=\"o_594c3fb181015d44876b\" data-key-why=\"Hemodynamic compromise from PE is an indication to assess urgently for thrombolysis.\" data-d1-why=\"An unstable patient should not wait for an unsafe CT transfer.\" data-d2-why=\"Anticoagulation alone does not rapidly relieve the obstructing clot in a shock presentation.\">62 yo F with suspected PE, hypotensive with right ventricular strain → <b>Thrombolysis</b></li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Deep vein thrombosis\" data-d2=\"Ruptured Baker cyst\" data-item-id=\"q_88073c6c98a455ea8db0\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_3bda73feea7c56d195a3\" data-d1-id=\"o_ba5d77783e6e5dae8f04\" data-d2-id=\"o_9f1d167131b8571297d5\" data-key-why=\"Fever with spreading skin inflammation favors cellulitis.\" data-d1-why=\"Diffuse unilateral swelling with thrombotic risk and calf tenderness.\" data-d2-why=\"Sudden calf pain with knee disease; bruising can track below the malleolus.\">62 yo F with a warm erythematous calf, fever, and no swelling gradient → <b>Cellulitis</b></li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Deep vein thrombosis\" data-d2=\"Superficial thrombophlebitis\" data-item-id=\"q_69959453b4a55a53924b\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_7ab9d4112bd9522b92bd\" data-d1-id=\"o_3e087a4633d25a339713\" data-d2-id=\"o_cede6c869c415867b01d\" data-key-why=\"A crescent bruise below the malleolus after sudden calf pain favors cyst rupture.\" data-d1-why=\"Diffuse unilateral swelling with thrombotic risk and calf tenderness.\" data-d2-why=\"A tender, palpable cord along a superficial vein.\">62 yo F with sudden calf pain and ecchymosis below the malleolus → <b>Ruptured Baker cyst</b></li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"pearls\"><span class=\"lbl\">Pearls</span> <span class=\"mask\">ECG (electrocardiogram) may show sinus tachycardia. S1Q3T3 means an S wave in lead I, a Q wave in lead III and T-wave inversion in lead III; it is an insensitive and only moderately specific pattern, so use the probability-based diagnostic workup. Treatment depends on stability, provoking factors and bleeding risk.</span> Contraceptive eligibility is owned by <a href=\"#contraception\">Contraception</a>.</div>\n<div class=\"traps\"><div class=\"trapline\"><span class=\"pill p-test\">Test-overrides-findings</span><span class=\"trapwhy\">D-dimer: it rises with infection, malignancy, pregnancy and surgery, so a positive result confirms nothing; <span class=\"mask\">with high pretest probability, go straight to imaging.</span></span></div></div>\n</div>",
   "ledger": "repair/migration/fm/dvt/spine/claim_map.json",
   "note": "s154c pause point blocks; shipped baseline preserved"
